  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Inside a space-path formation with yellow sky and purple sand ground, Fang Yuan briefly picks out immortal beans among scribe grass, nutrient peaches, blood tide flowers, and dozens of other immortal materials. Most of those materials are rank six, with a few at rank seven, and their quantity is shocking. He later notes that immortal beans grow in spring water, yet here they grow on the purple sand instead, which is one of several signs that the field is wrong. When materials leave that sand they wither into purple sand and are unusable.",
      "chapters": [
        934
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-among-immortal-materials",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Di Chang is sealed into the painting of Divine Bean Palace and sees a grey-white land with deep pits where he had planted immortal beans. Most of the beans have already been used up in the fight, leaving only sprouts slowly growing.",
